title: The Budget
subtitle: The Republic must pay for the year ahead.
tags: event
view-if: budget_due and not new_session and not finale and not game_ending
priority: 2
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_trade.svg
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetOpen(Q); !}

= The Budget of [+ bby +] BBY

The treasury holds **[+ treasury_txt +]**, and the Republic owes the InterGalactic Banking Clan **[+ debt_txt +]** ([+ debt_label +]). Trade along the hyperlanes is [+ trade_label +], which brings in about [+ bd_income_base +] before any new revenue. Running the Republic and its forces costs [+ bd_upkeep +], and interest comes to [+ bd_interest +].

The guilds' patience is [+ gp_label +]; our Core patrons are [+ pg_label +].

[? if bd_write : The Caucus [? if rc_chancellor : holds the Chancellery?][? if not rc_chancellor : chairs the Finance & Commerce Committee?], so we write this year's budget, but it must still pass the Senate. First: how will the Republic raise money? ?][? if not bd_write : The government proposes to [+ bd_gov_text +]. On present form it would win about [+ bd_gov_outlook +]% of the Senate. ?]

*Every source of money has people who pay for it, and they push back harder each year it is used in a row. Every budget must pass the Senate, where each bloc judges what it costs their own worlds.*

- @rev_tariffs: Trade-route tariffs (about [+ bd_tariff_yield +]).
- @rev_levy: A levy on the Core worlds (3).
- @rev_loan: Borrow from the Banking Clan (3).
- @rev_bonds: Sell war bonds (about [+ bd_bond_yield +]).
- @rev_spice: Collect the spice duty (2).
- @rev_print: Debase the Republic credit (4).
- @rev_none: No new revenue: existing taxes only.
- @support: Support the government's budget.
- @oppose: Vote against it.
- @amend: Demand a different spending priority.

@rev_tariffs
view-if: bd_write
subtitle: The guilds' patience wears thinner[? if rev_streak_tariffs >= 1 : , faster than last year?]; shippers pass the cost on to the Rim. The guilds will vote against it. [? if bd_brkn_rev_tariffs : **[+ bd_brk_rev_tariffs +]** ?]
choose-if: date >= tariff_ban_until
unavailable-subtitle: We promised the guilds no new tariffs for now.
on-arrival: bd_rev = "tariffs"
go-to: priority

@rev_levy
view-if: bd_write
subtitle: Our own Core patrons pay it[? if rev_streak_levy >= 1 : , for another year?]: their goodwill and donations fall, and the Moderates vote against. [? if bd_brkn_rev_levy : **[+ bd_brk_rev_levy +]** ?]
choose-if: date >= levy_ban_until
unavailable-subtitle: We promised the Core no new levy for now.
on-arrival: bd_rev = "levy"
go-to: priority

@rev_loan
view-if: bd_write
subtitle: Painless now, and the guilds approve. The debt grows, and so does the Banking Clan's leverage. [? if bd_brkn_rev_loan : **[+ bd_brk_rev_loan +]** ?]
on-arrival: bd_rev = "loan"
go-to: priority

@rev_bonds
view-if: bd_write and war
subtitle: [? if faith >= 45 : Faith in the Republic is high enough to sell them. ?][? if faith < 45 : Faith in the Republic is low: the drive may fail, in public. ?] [? if bd_brkn_rev_bonds : **[+ bd_brk_rev_bonds +]** ?]
on-arrival: bd_rev = "bonds"
go-to: priority

@rev_spice
view-if: bd_write and spice_legal
subtitle: Easy money from the Kessel trade. Corruption grows, and the syndicates' money goes where it likes. [? if bd_brkn_rev_spice : **[+ bd_brk_rev_spice +]** ?]
on-arrival: bd_rev = "spice"
go-to: priority

@rev_print
view-if: bd_write
subtitle: The most money, for now. Prices rise, the Rim suffers first, Core savers turn on us, and if it goes too far the Rim stops using Republic credits. [? if bd_brkn_rev_print : **[+ bd_brk_rev_print +]** ?]
on-arrival: bd_rev = "print"
go-to: priority

@rev_none
view-if: bd_write
subtitle: No one is angered; the treasury will have to manage on trade and existing taxes. [? if bd_brkn_rev_none : **[+ bd_brk_rev_none +]** ?]
on-arrival: bd_rev = "none"
go-to: priority

@support
view-if: not bd_write
subtitle: Our votes go to the government's budget. If it passes, the government is grateful[? if rc_in_govt : , and the coalition calmer?]. [? if bd_gov_breaks_n : **[+ bd_gov_breaks +]** ?]
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetPropose(Q, Q.bd_gov_rev, Q.bd_gov_pri, 1, 0); if (!Q.bd_failed) { Q[Q.chancellor_bloc + '_relation'] += 2; if (Q.rc_in_govt) Q.coalition_dissent -= 0.5; } !}
go-to: budget_result

@oppose
view-if: not bd_write
subtitle: If it fails, a stopgap passes: no new revenue and no priorities. The government will not forgive it.
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetPropose(Q, Q.bd_gov_rev, Q.bd_gov_pri, 0, 0); Q[Q.chancellor_bloc + '_relation'] -= 4; if (Q.rc_in_govt) Q.coalition_dissent += 1; if (Q.bd_failed) { Q.faith -= 0.5; Q.rc_momentum += 0.3; } !}
go-to: budget_result

@amend
view-if: not bd_write and rc_in_govt
subtitle: −1 political capital. We keep the government's revenue plan but choose what it pays for.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: {! Q.capital -= 1; Q.bd_rev = Q.bd_gov_rev; Q[Q.chancellor_bloc + '_relation'] -= 2; !}
go-to: priority

@priority
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetPriorityOutlook(Q); !}

= What Will the Republic Pay For?

Choose one priority for the year. The treasury has [+ treasury_txt +], with upkeep of [+ bd_upkeep +] and interest of [+ bd_interest +] to cover; anything we cannot pay, the Banking Clan will lend. Each option shows roughly how much of the Senate would back the whole budget.

- @pri_relief: Rim relief and hyperlane patrols (3).
- @pri_defence: Defence ([+ bd_defence_cost +]).
- @pri_subsidies: Subsidies for the Core and the guilds (2).
- @pri_repay: Repay the Banking Clan (3).
- @pri_none: Nothing new: balance the books.

@pri_relief
subtitle: Less hardship on the Rim, busier trade lanes, Rim donors for the Caucus; the Core grumbles. Expected support [+ bd_out_relief +]%. [? if bd_brkn_relief : **[+ bd_brk_relief +]** ?]
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetPropose(Q, Q.bd_rev, 'relief', 1, Q.bd_write); !}
go-to: budget_result

@pri_defence
subtitle: Stronger Judicial Forces[? if war : , with help for the weakest front?]; the Pacifists object and Tibanna grows dearer. Expected support [+ bd_out_defence +]%. [? if bd_brkn_defence : **[+ bd_brk_defence +]** ?]
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetPropose(Q, Q.bd_rev, 'defence', 1, Q.bd_write); !}
go-to: budget_result

@pri_subsidies
subtitle: The guilds' patience and our Core patrons recover; corruption grows and the Rimward wing objects. Expected support [+ bd_out_subsidies +]%. [? if bd_brkn_subsidies : **[+ bd_brk_subsidies +]** ?]
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetPropose(Q, Q.bd_rev, 'subsidies', 1, Q.bd_write); !}
go-to: budget_result

@pri_repay
subtitle: The debt shrinks, and with it the Banking Clan's grip. Expected support [+ bd_out_repay +]%. [? if bd_brkn_repay : **[+ bd_brk_repay +]** ?]
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetPropose(Q, Q.bd_rev, 'repay', 1, Q.bd_write); !}
go-to: budget_result

@pri_none
subtitle: No new spending this year[? if budget_pri = "relief" : , and the Rim will feel its relief cut?]. Expected support [+ bd_out_none +]%. [? if bd_brkn_none : **[+ bd_brk_none +]** ?]
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetPropose(Q, Q.bd_rev, 'none', 1, Q.bd_write); !}
go-to: budget_result

@budget_result
new-page: true

= The Budget Vote

[+ vote_html +]

*How the blocs lined up:* [+ bd_stances +].

[? if bd_failed : The budget is defeated. A stopgap keeps the Republic running: no new revenue, no new priorities. ?][? if not bd_failed : The Republic will raise money through **[+ bd_rev_name +]** and spend on **[+ bd_pri_name +]**. ?]

**How the galaxy reacts**

[+ bd_reactions +]

[+ bd_summary +]. The treasury now holds [+ treasury_txt +], and the debt stands at [+ debt_txt +] ([+ debt_label +]).
